.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-analyze 1  "pvc-analyze " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-analyze \- Phase vocoder analysis only: writes a `.pva` frame file, no resynthesis
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-analyze\fR [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Phase vocoder analysis only: writes a `.pva` frame file, no resynthesis.
.PP
Ports `pvanalysis`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ pvanalysis.c`) \- see `pvc\-core::tools::analyze`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope. Always writes the new `PVA1` format (see `pvc_io::pva`\*(Aqs module doc comment) \- never the legacy layout, which is a read\-only oracle\-comparison format here.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]
FFT size (must be a power of two)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 4096]
Analysis window length. Defaults to `4096` \- the C\*(Aqs own hardcoded default, *not* `2 * fft` (same gotcha as `pv`\*(Aqs `\-\-window\-size`; see `pvc\-core::tools::analyze`\*(Aqs doc comment). Pass `0` for the `2 * fft` auto\-scaling rule instead
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]
Analysis window shape
.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]
Analysis frames per second (sets the hop size)
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Low shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
High shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
Low shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
High shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\fR \fI<WARP>\fR [default: 0]
Spectrum magnitude warp index (`0` = no warp)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

